# qtd Build & Test skill

Use this skill when working on qtd to ensure correct build/test/code-quality workflow.

## Build

```sh
cmake -B build/opencode -S .
cmake --build build/opencode --target qtd
cmake --build build/opencode            # build all (including tests)
```

## Test

Run backend tests first (faster):
```sh
ctest --test-dir build/opencode -LE frontend-test -j8 --output-on-failure
```

Then frontend tests:
```sh
ctest --test-dir build/opencode -L frontend-test -j8 --output-on-failure
```

Or run all at once:
```sh
ctest --test-dir build/opencode --output-on-failure -j8
```

## Code quality checks (run after editing)

### clang-tidy per file
```sh
clang-tidy -p build/opencode --config-file .clang-tidy path/to/edited/file.cpp
```

### Verification scripts
```sh
bash scripts/verify_license_headers.sh
bash scripts/verify_no_quuid_usage.sh
bash scripts/verify_no_include_guards.sh
```

## Coverage (GCC build + gcovr required)

```sh
cmake --build build/opencode --target coverage
cmake --build build/opencode --target verify-test-coverage
```
